FUNCTION-=====>

1->
Function declaration- Writing name of program.
Syntax:
data_type function_name(datatype argument);

2->
Function definition- Writing body of function.
Syntax:
data_type function_name(datatype argument);
{
    function body;
}

3->
Function calling- Call the function.
Syntax:
function_name(argument_list);

4->
Function Syntax Example:

#include<stdio.h>
void fun();    // FUNCTION DECLARATION

void main()
{
    fun();     //FUNCTION CALLING
}

void fun()    //FUNCTION DEFINITION
{
    printf("This is body of function:");
} 
   
